COPY public.page_content (id, page_name, section_name, title, subtitle, content, background_image, created_at, updated_at, title_am, subtitle_am, content_am) FROM stdin;
3	about	hero	The Adwa Museum stands as Ethiopia's premier historical institution, dedicated to preserving and sharing the remarkable story of the Battle of Adwa.			https://adwavictorymemorial.gov.et/api/uploads/content-images/539fccc089a3b989334c96b6d977fac2	2025-08-24 01:22:22.819349	2026-07-22 10:05:33.789463		\N	\N
4	about	content_section	Our Story		Erected as a monument of global historic significance, the Adwa Victory Memorial is a state-of-the-art institution designed to chronicle Africa's ultimate triumph over colonial expansion. The complex, situated in Addis Ababa’s historic Piassa district adjacent to the City Administration, represents a major cultural milestone constructed by the Addis Ababa City Administration under the conceptual initiative of Prime Minister Dr. Abiy Ahmed. It serves not merely as a repository of the past, but as a dynamic space dedicated to safeguarding the nation's ancestral heritage and fostering civic pride.\r\nAt its core, the institution honors the monumental events of March 1, 1896. Through meticulously curated exhibition halls, it traces the strategic brilliance, unyielding resilience, and absolute unity that defined the Battle of Adwa. The memorial provides an in-depth exploration of the leadership of Emperor Menelik II, Empress Taytu Betul, and the twelve heroic generals who commanded the Ethiopian forces. By preserving these priceless archives and artifacts, the institution offers global visitors a profound understanding of how a united populace successfully defended its national sovereignty, forever altering the course of global history and inspiring modern pan-African liberation.\r\nToday, the facility functions as a premier educational, research, and diplomatic hub within the continent's capital. By integrating extensive archival repositories for international scholars with versatile public infrastructures, such as the grand 2,500-seat Pan African Hall, multi-purpose amphitheaters, and indoor athletic venues, the memorial fosters a unique environment where historical education meets contemporary civic life. It stands as a permanent testament to the enduring power of determination, dignity, and sovereignty for generations to come.	\N	2025-08-24 01:22:22.819349	2026-07-22 10:05:33.914041	ታሪካችን	\N	
1	home	hero	Adwa Victory Memorial 	The Triumph of Unity 		https://adwavictorymemorial.gov.et/api/uploads/content-images/6047b56931796bd06c84cb94cd215db2	2025-08-24 01:22:22.819349	2026-06-28 10:21:24.609624	የዓድዋ  ድል መታሰቢያ	የአንድነት ድል	
2	home	about_section	A Living Testament to African Resilience and Glory		Majestically perched in the historic center of Addis Ababa (Piassa) near the City Administration complex, the Adwa Victory Memorial stands as a grand, first-of-its-kind landmark in African history. Built by the Addis Ababa City Administration through the visionary initiative of Prime Minister Dr. Abiy Ahmed, this ultra-modern architectural masterpiece significantly elevates the beauty of Addis Ababa, the proud diplomatic capital of Africa.\r\nStep inside and embark on an extraordinary journey through one of world history’s most defining moments. The memorial permanently commemorates the historic Battle of Adwa on March 1, 1896, where Ethiopia’s decisive victory over colonial forces ensured national sovereignty and ignited the flame of liberation across the African continent.\r\nWhat to Explore:\r\n    • The Immersive Museum: Experience the historic triumph through cutting-edge interactive technology, priceless authentic artifacts, and the inspiring stories of Emperor Menelik II, Empress Taytu Betul, and the heroic generals.\r\n    • World-Class Facilities: Tour the magnificent Pan African Hall (hosting up to 2,500 guests), state-of-the-art theaters, an amphitheater, and a comprehensive research center for global scholars.\r\n    • Vibrant Community Spaces: Enjoy modern indoor sporting venues, a gymnasium, green spaces, and cafes designed to bridge our ancestral heroism with future possibilities.\r\nThe Adwa Victory Memorial is more than a museum, it is a living symbol of pride, unity, and resilience for generations to come.\r\n	\N	2025-08-24 01:22:22.819349	2026-06-28 10:21:26.874678	የኢትዮጵያ ክብር ሕያው ምስክር		
\.
